-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Binary distributions are GPL-3.0-or-later
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

padMule's own source is GPL-2.0-or-later, as stated above and in LICENSE.

However, padMule links the `ring` cryptography crate (via rustls, for HTTPS
server-list fetching, added 2026-08-10). `ring` is licensed "Apache-2.0 AND
ISC", and the Apache License 2.0 is NOT compatible with GPL-2.0-only - its
patent-termination clause conflicts. Apache-2.0 IS compatible with GPL-3.0.

Because padMule is GPL-2.0-OR-LATER, this is resolved by the "or later" option:
**a compiled padMule binary that includes `ring` is conveyed under
GPL-3.0-or-later.** The source remains GPL-2.0-or-later; the combined binary
work is GPL-3.0-or-later.

This is stated explicitly rather than left implicit because it is a real
constraint on redistribution, not a formality. Anyone who needs padMule under
GPL-2.0-only must build without `ring` - today that means replacing the rustls
crypto provider. The `deny.toml` license policy carries the same reasoning and
will fail CI if a future dependency introduces a license that breaks this.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Derivation and third-party code
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

padMule is a port of aMule to iPadOS. The engine is a Rust rewrite (crates/), and
the native shell is SwiftUI (ios/). It derives from, and in places ports code
and on-disk/wire formats from:

  aMule 3.0.1
    Copyright (C) The aMule Team and contributors
    Licensed GPL-2.0-or-later.
    The upstream source is vendored, unmodified, under amule-3.0.1/ and serves as
    the reference oracle for this port. Its own license, authors, and credits are
    preserved there:
      amule-3.0.1/LICENSE.md      (GNU GPL v2)
      amule-3.0.1/docs/COPYING    (GNU GPL v2, identical to this repo's LICENSE)
      amule-3.0.1/docs/AUTHORS.md (the aMule Team)

  aMule itself descends from eMule (GPL-2.0-or-later, (C) the eMule Team). Where
  padMule follows eMule 0.50a as the wire/format authority, that too is GPL code.

Because padMule reuses and ports GPL-2.0-or-later code, padMule as a whole is
licensed GPL-2.0-or-later. Any file borrowed from aMule, eMule, or another fork
keeps its original copyright and license notices.
